From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 04:23:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: the desk packs no WebUI it cannot open

The desk runs Chrome as an --app window with no tab strip, toolbar or
side panel, and no <webview> may navigate to chrome:// (patch 0083). So
Chrome's settings, New Tab page, password manager, tab search, side
panels, What's New and the WebUI gallery are pages nothing can reach.

- chrome_paks.gni leaves their paks out of resources.pak.
- chrome_web_ui_configs.cc no longer registers the full pages among them
  (Settings, the New Tab page and its third-party variant, the password
  manager, What's New, the gallery), so the linker can drop their
  controllers and handlers.
- The ones Chrome opens in its own top-chrome views (tab search, the side
  panels, Customize Chrome) stay registered: something may still preload
  them, and an empty page is safer there than a missing config.
---
 .../browser/ui/webui/chrome_web_ui_configs.cc |  6 ------
 chrome/chrome_paks.gni                        | 21 +------------------
 2 files changed, 1 insertion(+), 26 deletions(-)

